<heading>dig - Create a box and connect to it.</heading>
<rule/>
<heading level="2">Usage</heading>
<pre>dig NAME
dig NAME --direction north
dig NAME --direction east --twoway
dig NAME --world NLP</pre>
<heading level="2">Description</heading>
<paragraph>Creates a new box and connects it to the current box via an exit. If a box with the given name already exists, only the exit is created. The box is created in the current world by default; use --world to create (or find) it in another world.</paragraph>
<heading level="2">Examples</heading>
<pre>dig Garden
  Create a box and connect to it.
dig Office --direction east
  Create a box with a directional exit.
dig Basement --direction down --twoway
  Create a two-way connection.
dig Portals --world NLP
  Create a box in the NLP world and connect to it.</pre>
<heading level="2">See also</heading>
<paragraph>connect, enter, go, leave, look, place</paragraph>
